1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,743
If you run research for a small business, the useful AI question is

2
00:00:05,743 --> 00:00:11,487
practical: can it help you answer one business question, with evidence you can

3
00:00:11,487 --> 00:00:17,230
check, at an effort you can afford? This brief proposes a bounded customer-synthesis

4
00:00:17,230 --> 00:00:22,974
pilot. Start with research material you already hold, name the person responsible for

5
00:00:22,974 --> 00:00:28,717
interpretation, and compare the full workload with your current manual process. This is

6
00:00:28,717 --> 00:00:34,019
an editorial proposal, not a tested intervention or a promise of savings.

7
00:00:36,019 --> 00:00:42,168
Nielsen Norman Group makes a useful distinction: asking AI to organize research you

8
00:00:42,168 --> 00:00:48,318
have is different from asking it to generate evidence you do not possess.

9
00:00:48,318 --> 00:00:54,467
For a pilot, that means working from retained interview notes, survey responses, or

10
00:00:54,467 --> 00:01:00,617
support tickets. Every proposed finding should point back to its source. If you

11
00:01:00,617 --> 00:01:06,766
cannot locate that support, label the finding as an assumption. A polished summary

12
00:01:06,766 --> 00:01:12,916
is not enough. Check whether its themes preserve what participants actually said, including

13
00:01:12,916 --> 00:01:19,065
contradictions and outliers. Synthetic customer statements cannot stand in for observed customer evidence.

14
00:01:21,065 --> 00:01:27,343
What counts as success? In Greenbook’s interview, Wex practitioner Nadine van Rooyen argues

15
00:01:27,343 --> 00:01:33,621
that an insight’s success should not depend solely on whether its recommendation gets

16
00:01:33,621 --> 00:01:39,899
implemented. That gives a small-business pilot a useful question: did the checked findings

17
00:01:39,899 --> 00:01:46,177
improve understanding of the decision, even if the business chose to wait? But

18
00:01:46,177 --> 00:01:52,455
Wex is a global enterprise with specialist roles. This practitioner account does not

19
00:01:52,455 --> 00:01:57,284
establish small-business return on investment, staffing requirements, or AI effectiveness.

20
00:01:59,284 --> 00:02:06,095
Context also takes work. In Insight Platforms’ interview, South African researcher Mpho Mpofu

21
00:02:06,095 --> 00:02:12,906
calls for budgets to accommodate language and cultural context. For your pilot, identify

22
00:02:12,906 --> 00:02:19,717
who can check local meaning, and include that effort in the comparison. Do

23
00:02:19,717 --> 00:02:26,527
not assume an English summary captures every nuance. Mpofu’s perspective concerns varied African

24
00:02:26,527 --> 00:02:33,338
markets. It should not become a single regional customer profile. These English-language interviews

25
00:02:33,338 --> 00:02:39,101
also do not directly represent non-English customers or small-business AI deployments.

26
00:02:41,101 --> 00:02:48,459
Together, these sources support our inference: assess traceability and contextual fit before treating

27
00:02:48,459 --> 00:02:55,817
AI outputs as decision evidence. Producing a recommendation, or getting it implemented, is

28
00:02:55,817 --> 00:03:03,175
insufficient by itself. Keep the pilot narrow. Record preparation, AI-assisted organization, human checking,

29
00:03:03,175 --> 00:03:10,532
corrections, and later maintenance. Compare those tasks with the current manual process, using

30
00:03:10,532 --> 00:03:17,890
the same question and material. Record actual costs rather than assuming savings. Name

31
00:03:17,890 --> 00:03:25,248
an interpretation owner. Preserve unresolved questions. Customer-data handling and consent need separate evidence

32
00:03:25,248 --> 00:03:32,606
before disclosure to a tool. Expand only if the comparison supports it. The

33
00:03:32,606 --> 00:03:38,832
sources reviewed here do not demonstrate that this pilot design works.

34
00:03:40,832 --> 00:03:47,689
Watch for independent small-business evaluations that disclose manual baselines, total costs, source coverage,

35
00:03:47,689 --> 00:03:54,546
multilingual checks, and failures. Those results are missing here, as are customers’ views

36
00:03:54,546 --> 00:04:01,403
on data use and documented unsuccessful small-business deployments. Read these perspectives with their

37
00:04:01,403 --> 00:04:08,261
incentives in mind: Mpofu has book, research-business, and training interests; Greenbook promotes conferences;

38
00:04:08,261 --> 00:04:15,118
Insight Platforms operates a directory and conferences. The next step is a small,

39
00:04:15,118 --> 00:04:21,975
reviewable comparison. Keep the evidence, count the checking, and judge whether the work

40
00:04:21,975 --> 00:04:28,833
helps the decision. Codex assisted with drafting this script from the cited sources.
